        <h2>Turning a Clipboard-Only Capture Into a File</h2>

        <ol class="pl-5 space-y-2 steps-list">
            <li>Take your screenshot with <strong>Win + Shift + S</strong> and select your region, or press <strong>PrtScn</strong> for the full screen.</li>
            <li>Open <a href="https://pastedownloadapp.com/">pastedownloadapp.com</a> in a new tab. No sign-up, no install.</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Ctrl + V</strong> to paste the clipboard image onto the page.</li>
            <li>Choose your format: PNG for lossless quality, JPG for a smaller file. The <a href="/blog/png-vs-jpg-vs-webp/">PNG vs JPG vs WebP comparison</a> covers WebP too.</li>
            <li>Click <strong>Download</strong> and the file saves to your downloads folder.</li>
        </ol>

